The photo shows a square white plate holding a small mixed green salad: spinach leaves with shredded carrot, and red leaf lettuce with a few blackberries. It looks lightly dressed.

The plate is about 24 cm across, so it reads as a dinner-size plate. The salad covers only a small part of it and is a thin layer of leaves. I estimate about 70 g of greens plus a little dressing, so roughly 80 g in total. Greens contribute about 15 kcal, and the dressing and berries add perhaps 50 kcal, for about 65 kcal overall. I'll round up slightly to allow for extra dressing.

